-- The pairing tower rows (S8c). Each row compares one def of the Fp2, Fp6
-- and Fp12 tower of domain/domain.lang with the value of the C oracle
-- (test/cryptotool.c, pf_rows) on the fixture states pfA and pfB. The Words
-- of a row are the value of the oracle: each Fe is 8 Words in Montgomery
-- form, least significant first, in the order of the fp2, fp6 and fp12
-- constructors. A row gives 1 when the def gives the value of the oracle.
-- A name that ends in C uses the native product feMulC. A name that ends in
-- G uses the guest product feMul. A Ne row gives 1 when f2Eq, f6Eq or f12Eq
-- refuses a value that is different from the state in one part only.
-- `langc --kit eval` evaluates each def of the file at load, also below
-- binders. Thus a term that is heavy at load is a cost of each row of the
-- file. A row gives its product to the tower def through the gate prGM, and
-- a power row gives its bits through the gate prGB. Each gate takes the
-- first Word w0 of the row. A gate does not reduce while w0 is a variable,
-- thus the products and the powers do not start at load.
-- One row for the power by bnXBits is above the arena limit of langc. Thus
-- that power is 2 step rows, prF12PowXa and prF12PowXb (see the Fp12 rows).
-- The G2 rows compare the point and line defs of domain/domain.lang
-- (p2OnCurve to lineAdd) with the oracle (pf_point_rows) on the fixtures
-- pfP, pfQ, pfQBad and pfT8. A Pt2 row has 32 Words (x, then y). A Jac2 row
-- has 48 Words (x, y, then z). A line row has 96 Words (one Fp12). A test
-- row has 1 Word (0, the gate). The oracle gives the C test (1 for yes, 0
-- for no), and the row gives 1 when the test of the def gives yes.
-- This is a kit file outside the Wasm set. test/gate.sh evaluates each row
-- with `langc --kit eval`.
